# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://goauthentik.io/blueprints/schema.json
# ── nOS SSO autologin flow — sso-autologin-plan.md Batch 5 (Authentik branding) ──
#
# The "Authentik branded flow" FALLBACK half of the custom-preloader work
# (the Wing /hub splash is the PRIMARY; this is the first-login polish lever
# the plan calls Option A). It converges a dedicated authorization flow
# `nos-autologin-flow` that `autologin: true` clients route their
# `authorization_flow` at — INSTEAD of the stock
# `default-provider-authorization-implicit-consent` — see 10-oidc-apps.yaml.j2.
#
# DESIGN — Dummy stage + per-flow background + Custom CSS (per plan §"Vazba na
# Authentik branding"):
#   - NO custom stage class. A custom stage would require a Python plugin
#     shipped INTO the Authentik server image — we keep this pure-YAML so a
#     stock authentik image converges cleanly (same doctrine as the enrollment
#     flow's "why a policy, not a custom stage" note).
#   - NO image bloat. The brandable splash is the FLOW BACKGROUND + Custom CSS
#     on the flow itself (Authentik renders `flow.background` + `flow.layout`
#     and Brand-level Custom CSS ≥2025.4.0 over the consent/auth screen). We do
#     NOT embed a base64 image; the background path points at a brand asset the
#     operator drops in (default: the stock authentik background, so the flow is
#     visually a no-op until branded).
#   - A single Dummy stage (`authentik_stages_dummy.dummystage`) is the
#     no-op carrier the flow needs to be a valid, bindable flow object without
#     collecting any input. It throw-shows the branded background for the
#     ~100–200 ms repeat-login redirect (the only latency the preloader can
#     actually mask — first-login still runs the full upstream flow).
#
# ── HONESTY CAVEAT — implicit-consent silent-skip is NOT guaranteed ──────────
# The plan (and the research it folds in) WARNS that Authentik's
# implicit-consent silent-skip has documented regressions where the consent
# prompt STILL shows despite implicit consent — GH goauthentik/authentik
# #15814 (open/reviewing), #13068, #8660 — especially with the `offline_access`
# scope or on first login.
#
#   >>> OPERATOR STEP (load-bearing): before relying on a seamless one-click
#   >>> redirect, VERIFY end-to-end on YOUR installed Authentik version that
#   >>> this flow silently skips the consent screen for an already-authenticated
#   >>> session. If it does NOT, add an explicit `authentik_stages_consent.
#   >>> consentstage` (mode: permanent / expiring) bound into this flow AND an
#   >>> expression policy that skips the UI only when a session already exists,
#   >>> then reset the preloader messaging to set correct expectations.
#
# Implicit consent here = the flow carries NO consent stage (just the no-op
# Dummy stage), the plan's recommended-IF-VERIFIED variant. The flow is
# DORMANT: nothing routes `authorization_flow` here unless a
# client's `authentik.autologin.enabled` resolves true (gate-locked so
# `supports: no` services can never flip on), and the whole autologin mechanism
# is off behind `sso_autologin: false`. The flow object simply sits unused
# until a verified operator opts in.
#
# (NB: this header avoids literal Jinja brace-tags — Jinja parses them even
# inside YAML # comments, so a stray tag here would break the render.)
version: 1
metadata:
  name: nos-autologin-flow
  labels:
    managed-by: nos
    blueprint-version: "1"

entries:
  # ── 1. Dummy stage — pure no-op carrier (NO custom stage class) ───────────
  # The flow needs at least one bindable stage to be a valid flow object. A
  # dummy stage collects nothing and immediately continues; its sole job here
  # is to give the branded background + Custom CSS a surface to paint during
  # the brief repeat-login redirect. It never blocks and never prompts.
  - model: authentik_stages_dummy.dummystage
    state: present
    identifiers:
      name: nos-autologin-dummy
    attrs:
      throw_error: false

  # ── 2. The autologin authorization flow ───────────────────────────────────
  # designation: authorization  → eligible as a provider `authorization_flow`.
  # authentication: require_authenticated → an UNauthenticated hit bounces to
  #   the stock authentication flow first (so first-login still works); only an
  #   already-authenticated session reaches this flow and gets the silent skip.
  # layout/background → the brandable splash surface (per-flow background, the
  #   plan's "per-flow background" lever; operator overrides the asset).
  - model: authentik_flows.flow
    state: present
    identifiers:
      slug: nos-autologin-flow
    attrs:
      name: "nOS — SSO autologin (branded)"
      title: "Signing you in…"
      designation: authorization
      authentication: require_authenticated
      compatibility_mode: false
      denied_action: message_continue
      layout: stacked
      policy_engine_mode: any
      # Per-flow branded background. Default = stock authentik asset, so the
      # flow is a visual no-op until the operator drops a brand image here.
      # CAUTION (plan): keep this a PATH/asset reference — do NOT inline a
      # base64 image (image bloat). Operator brands via System > Brands
      # (flow background + Custom CSS, Authentik ≥2025.4.0).
      background: "{{ sso_autologin_flow_background | default('/static/dist/assets/images/flow_background.jpg') }}"

  # ── 3. Stage binding — the single Dummy stage at order 10 ─────────────────
  - model: authentik_flows.flowstagebinding
    state: present
    identifiers:
      target: !Find [authentik_flows.flow, [slug, nos-autologin-flow]]
      order: 10
    attrs:
      stage: !Find [authentik_stages_dummy.dummystage, [name, nos-autologin-dummy]]
      evaluate_on_plan: true
      re_evaluate_policies: false
      invalid_response_action: retry
      policy_engine_mode: any
